{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Rectangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n\t<mi>D</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> has an area of <math alttext=\"280\"><mn>280</mn>\n</math> square centimeters. The length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> centimeters. What is the width, in centimeters, of the rectangle?</p>", "keys": ["ee726695-f2cd-459f-a3b9-3c222537b6f2"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "318b6a63-8e9b-48ba-b0e1-b76d6732d1e4", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "ee726695-f2cd-459f-a3b9-3c222537b6f2", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "7aafa84f-3248-430d-8735-fe4d972586a1", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"76\"><mn>76</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "0b1c119f-a7a4-4cd3-b0d6-7b360cb38ce4", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"140\"><mn>140</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> of a rectangle is the product of its length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and its width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math>.&nbsp;It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> has an area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"280\"><mn>280</mn></math> square centimeters and the length of the rectangle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> centimeters. Substituting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"280\"><mn>280</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"280 equals 10 w\"><mn>280</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>w</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28 equals w\"><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></math>. Therefore, the width, in centimeters, of the rectangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the length, in centimeters, not the width, in centimeters, of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is half the area, in square centimeters, not the width, in centimeters, of the rectangle.</p>", "externalid": "5d25f220-0193-4939-a687-673246d3076b", "correct_answer": ["B"]}